{
  "caption": "The app's data, step by step, for an app that keeps a database and receipts. Before the first release Stage has a folder of its own. The first release can take Stage's data along. Production then builds up data alone. At every release hi forks production's data for Stage: files written once linked, the database copied. In Stage's box, the fork is read only and whatever Stage writes stays in its own folder. At the next release, what Stage wrote is kept once and Stage gets a new fork.",
